  "readmeFile": "NUGET.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First stable release. The libraries' public API is promised from here under semantic versioning: a breaking change waits for a new major version, and each release is checked against the last one published. Since 0.2.0-alpha it has only grown: EngineRegistry.DetectAt takes a story file as well as a folder or disc image, and DetectedGame.GameFile names the file a game was found in. The Z-machine interpreter is under the GPL with the rest of GUE, so the Gue.ZMachine package no longer carries an MIT licence. New in the player: --version. Plays Return to Zork's CD releases, Zork Nemesis and Zork: Grand Inquisitor (CD and DVD data) with their sound and saves, and Infocom's Z-machine games, versions 1 to 6, with Beyond Zork's and Zork Zero's pictures and the mouse. It gives the same output, to the byte, on Windows, Linux and macOS, where it has been played in its window, but for a few pixels of the Z-Vision games' panoramas. What it does not do is in the README under Known limitations.",
